# Build context hygiene, and the first line is the one that matters.
#
# `node_modules` must never enter the context: pnpm's store is a tree of symlinks
# into a content-addressed store with platform-specific binaries, so a Windows
# host's copy is not merely large but wrong inside a Linux image — and the
# Dockerfile installs its own. It is also the difference between a context measured
# in megabytes and one measured in gigabytes.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Secrets. `.env` holds a live database URL and a real Resend key; a build context
# is readable by anything that can run a build, and a file copied into a layer stays
# in that layer even if a later step deletes it. Environment reaches the container
# through docker-compose at run time instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output and caches — regenerated inside the image, and stale copies here
# would silently shadow a fresh build.
.next
dist
.turbo
build

# Test and tooling artifacts, none of which the API needs to run.
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
coverage
apps/web/test-results
apps/web/playwright-report

# Local scratch that has no business in an image.
.tmp
.tmp-db-query.cjs
.web-preview.log
outputs

# VCS and editor state. `.git` in particular is both large and pointless here.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Documentation. Excluded because it changes constantly and would bust the build
# cache on every edit while contributing nothing to a running API.
*.md
docs
